    "omicsSubtype": "bulk-rna-seq",
    "analytical_narrative": "The dataset is raw STAR/featureCounts gene counts (12,000 genes x 11 samples) from 5 human subjects, each contributing one control and one treated blood sample (paired design). The treatment effect must therefore be estimated within subjects: a subject blocking term before the condition term removes between-subject variance from the test (DESeq2 design ~ subject + condition, Wald test, apeglm-shrunken log2FC, BH at alpha 0.05 with independent filtering). Sample-structure QC (blind VST, PCA, distance heatmap) runs first to verify pairing integrity and detect outliers; counts are only minimally pre-filtered (>=10 counts in >=5 samples). A final report step carries the gene table, MA and dispersion diagnostics, a DESeq2-vs-edgeR-QL robustness overlap (treated as high-confidence intersection), and a full reproducibility record. No pathway or translational work is planned: the question asks only for the treatment-responsive genes."
  },
